f bug that survives\r\n# until someone runs the suite on a stock Windows install.\r\n2308:[interface.IF-305]\r\n2313:data = \"[--session ID] [--root DIR]; ambient home and session selection; recorded, unchanged, open, skipped, refused, absent, parent-unresolved stdout; exits 0, 1, 2\"\r\nproject-trajectory/scripts/session_adapters.py:668:    if messages and not messages[-1].stopped:\nproject-trajectory/scripts/session_adapters.py:669:        return tuple(messages[:-1]), messages[-1].id\ndocs/requirements/system-requirements.toml:1954:acceptance_criteria = \"Every coordinated session and nested agent is recorded with its identity; usage counts each completed message once, marks source-stated partial counts, and adds nothing on repeated, resumed, or interrupted recording; a session already recorded by the service is not counted twice; an ingested record has no gate authority and contains no transcript text; an unknown source shape is refused naming the defect; and published coordination guidance runs the recording at close-out and at a headless leg's end, including pickup of the previous session's tail.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
