{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"@'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path('C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-10-22c-leg13/r1/sol/wi-961-57067b9-full-review.md')\np.write_text('''Reviewed: 57067b9fc6bf61f4d6c2f02353b38522989ecf49\n\nVerified: Independently exercised the transcript reader and actual usage_ingest.main -> session_service.record -> spool flow, reviewed WI-961 and its specref against the scoped diff, and checked the cited requirement relationships. The prescribed 122 tests pass, trajectory is clean, and strict integrity reports zero orphans and integrity findings. Nested identities, repeated records, incremental contributions, service exclusion, privacy and gate isolation have useful behavioral tests. The worktree remains clean. The worst failure classes examined were silent usage loss/misattribution, duplicate accounting, and record overwrite/recovery failure. A completed-handback accounting gap remains.\n\nCoverage and semantic decisions:\n\n- Reader Done-when: nested identities and unique-message sums are covered by test_a_session_with_nested_agents_yields_four_invocations_with_their_identities, test_each_invocation_usage_is_its_unique_message_sum, test_a_repeated_record_adds_nothing and test_the_parents_tool_result_summary_is_never_read. The sum promise is UNCOVERED for completed handbacks without stop records; the whole CHAIN fixture reproduces the violation below. The depth test currently expects their omission.\n- Unknown shape: test_an_unknown_shape_is_refused_naming_file_and_field and test_an_unknown_shape_exits_nonzero_and_records_nothing_for_that_transcript exercise the reader and command, including malformed/missing fields and missing metas. These are genuine external-input boundary validations. Unsupported layouts fail closed; expanding them is a coverage extension, not a finding here.\n- Exactly once: repeated, appended